KMSDRM: release the locked GBM buffers before destroying the EGL surface.

Backport of upstream SDL commit 9cc2f248f5437daaf090e3ef6afb4f6dc88068ac
("kmsdrm: Fix order of GBM and EGL teardown", Cameron Gutman, SDL2 branch,
2026-04-11), unchanged.

KMSDRM_DestroySurfaces() destroyed the EGL surface and only then returned the
two locked front buffers with gbm_surface_release_buffer(). In Mesa's GBM
platform the buffer bookkeeping lives in the EGL surface:
dri2_drm_destroy_surface() frees the dri2_egl_surface and leaves the GBM
surface's dri_private pointing at it, and release_buffer() reads
dri_private->color_buffers[] (and clears a `locked` flag in it on a match).
So every teardown with buffers locked -- any exit or VT switch after two swaps
-- read and possibly wrote freed memory. With glibc the freed block is
usually still mapped and the access goes unnoticed; libphoenix's allocator
unmaps a heap as soon as its last block is freed, and SuperTuxKart's exit
took a translation fault in release_buffer
(docs/misc/2026-09-28-stk-scaled-exit-fault.md). Upstream hit the same
use-after-free in libnvidia-egl-gbm.so.

Release the buffers first, then destroy the EGL surface, then the GBM
surface. The mid-run recreation through KMSDRM_CreateSurfaces() is not
affected: it runs before the first swap, with no buffer locked. Not
Phoenix-specific.

--- a/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmvideo.c
+++ b/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmvideo.c
@@ -1115,17 +1115,6 @@
     }
 
     /***************************/
-    /* Destroy the EGL surface */
-    /***************************/
-
-    SDL_EGL_MakeCurrent(_this, EGL_NO_SURFACE, EGL_NO_CONTEXT);
-
-    if (windata->egl_surface != EGL_NO_SURFACE) {
-        SDL_EGL_DestroySurface(_this, windata->egl_surface);
-        windata->egl_surface = EGL_NO_SURFACE;
-    }
-
-    /***************************/
     /* Destroy the GBM buffers */
     /***************************/
 
@@ -1140,6 +1129,17 @@
     }
 
     /***************************/
+    /* Destroy the EGL surface */
+    /***************************/
+
+    SDL_EGL_MakeCurrent(_this, EGL_NO_SURFACE, EGL_NO_CONTEXT);
+
+    if (windata->egl_surface != EGL_NO_SURFACE) {
+        SDL_EGL_DestroySurface(_this, windata->egl_surface);
+        windata->egl_surface = EGL_NO_SURFACE;
+    }
+
+    /***************************/
     /* Destroy the GBM surface */
     /***************************/
 
